# Keep host build junk out of the frontend image context.
#
# Why this exists: artifacts/trash-the-test/Dockerfile runs `pnpm install`
# (Linux bins/links) and THEN copies sources over it. Without these excludes,
# a host-side `node_modules/` (Windows junctions/symlinks) and `dist/` get
# copied on top of the fresh container install and destroy the Linux vite
# binary links -> runtime crash:
#   Cannot find module '/repo/node_modules/.pnpm/vite@.../node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js'
#
# NOTE: `.env` is intentionally NOT excluded: the frontend Dockerfile has
# always baked it in and dev-server behavior must not change here. Compose
# additionally passes VITE_API_BASE_URL explicitly.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/coverage

.git
.gitignore
**/*.log
.DS_Store

pgdata
redisdata
tjdata
